NAVCORE-SoOP - JLCPCB order, from a phone
=========================================
Upload gerbers.zip as the PCB. Do NOT unzip it first.

FABRICATION
  Layers            6          <- if the preview shows 4, STOP. The power planes
                                  are missing and the board will not work.
  Dimensions        @@SIZE@@   (JLC reads it from the gerbers; it should agree)
  Delivery format   Panel by JLCPCB, 1 x 1, edge rails on all 4 sides, 12 mm
                                  <- about 70.5 x 71.2 mm, over JLC's 70 x 70 mm
                                  assembly minimum. NEVER 2 x 2: the servo headers
                                  hang 6.3 mm off the south edge (MMCX 2.2 mm north,
                                  microSD 1.3 mm west) and would sit over the next
                                  board; over a rail they are harmless. If only two
                                  rails are offered, 2 columns x 1 row with top and
                                  bottom rails. Do NOT upload a panel of your own.
  Depanel           No         <- the servo headers overhang the rail's cut line;
                                  snap the rails off by hand, away from the parts
  Thickness         1.6 mm
  Outer copper      1 oz       <- 0.5 oz halves every trace's current rating and
                                  invalidates kicad-tools irdrop.py check
  Inner copper      1 oz       <- the default 0.5 oz puts the VBAT plane on In4 at
                                  its current limit; irdrop.py check assumes 1 oz
  Surface finish    ENIG       <- 0402s and LGA parts want a flat finish
  Min track/space   4 mil (0.1016 mm)   should be free tier; an upcharge means
                                        the design rules drifted
  Min via / drill   0.45 / 0.20 mm
  Impedance control No
  Stackup           JLC's standard 6-layer 1.6 mm (JLC06161H-3313 or -2116): the
                                  1.6 GHz antenna line is 0.21 mm on a 0.1-0.12 mm
                                  outer prepreg. Ignore the stackup inside the gerber
                                  job file; it is KiCad's default, not the order.
  Via covering      Epoxy Filled & Capped   <- free on 6-layer boards and seals every
                                               via; @@VIAS_IN_PADS@@ vias sit inside SMD
                                               pads, so no joint depends on it
  Mark on PCB       "Remove Mark" (no order number). The silkscreen carries no
                    JLCJLCJLCJLC marker, so any other choice prints JLC's number
                    wherever it fits - possibly across a label. JLC may charge a
                    small fee for this; it is shown in the quote.

ASSEMBLY
  PCBA type         Standard   <- both sides populated, LGA IMUs; the parts list
                                  and the readiness manifest assume it
  Quantity          5 bare PCBs, 2 assembled  (5 is the multilayer minimum,
                    2 the SMT minimum; the 3 spare bare boards are the practice
                    pieces and cost almost nothing). With a 1 x 1 panel, panels
                    and boards are the same count.
  Side              BOTH sides are populated - @@SIDES@@. Two stencils.
  BOM               BOM-NAVCORE-SoOP.csv
  CPL               CPL-NAVCORE-SoOP.csv
  Placement preview Nothing should need turning. Every rotation and centre in the
                    CPL is fitted to JLCPCB's own footprint for that LCSC part
                    (kicad-tools fab.py orientation). A part that still shows turned
                    is a real finding - report it rather than just rotating it.
                    Look hardest at the parts a preview most often gets wrong:
                    pin 1 of U1, U2, U3, U13 and U31; ball A1 of U19 (a 1.5 x 1.0 mm
                    DSBGA that fits either way round); the cathode marks of D1, D2,
                    D3, D8 and D10.

  Variants, if you want them instead of the default:
    *-economic.csv  U3 (second IMU) left off for hand-fitting. That is the ONLY
                    difference from the default pair.

BEFORE YOU PAY - the things no offline check can confirm
  - Accept JLCPCB's free DFM review. It is the only thing that checks pad LAND
    SIZE and paste apertures; kicad-tools check.py footprints verifies pad count,
    package family and pitch, but not those.
  - Confirm the quote says 1 oz outer AND 1 oz inner copper.
  - ABSENT BY DESIGN, read straight out of the BOM in this bundle (ref + value):
@@DNP@@
    The placement preview must agree with that list exactly: a part on it that is
    placed, or a part that is placed and is not on it, means the wrong BOM went up.
  - SOLE SOURCE, from the dated stock snapshot in this repo. Confirm them in the
    quote tool and buy spares if the count looks tight:
      @@STOCK@@
    (MAX2112 is the tuner - nothing else in JLC's library covers 1616-1626.5 MHz
    with quadrature baseband output.)

WHAT THIS BOARD IS NOT, YET
  Ready to order is not ready to fly. tools/check_order.py rf fails until the T3b
  bench measurements exist, and U8/U9 junction temperatures are computed, not
  measured. See docs/navcore-runbook.pdf, Parts 7-10 (T1-T3a), before powering anything.
